        "raw": "<p>Hey all, quick simple question, I was trying out unity, haven&#39;t really played her much since I got her and I had a question about how modular workbench is played in regards to how her power can be played.</p><p>Modular Workbench - Discard 1 card. If you do, put 1 mech. golem from hand into play.</p><p>Unity&#39;s power - Destroy 1 equipment card.&nbsp; If you do, put a mech. golem from hand into play.</p><p>Now my question is, from reading spiffs doc. it says her power can destroy any equipment on the field, even if it isn&#39;t my own.&nbsp; Now if I play Modular Workbench, can anyone discard a card for me to play a golem?</p><p>I ask this because 1, i didn&#39;t see a link to the actual topic in spiffs doc. so i&#39;m unaware of the argument letting unity&#39;s power destory anyones equipment, so my arguement is that since the wording on the two cards are very simiular and it really isnt saying it can&#39;t be played this way, Whats stopping me from playing modular workbench that way?&nbsp;</p><p>Also I didnt find anything in the official rulebook saying I cant affect someone&#39;s hand this way.</p><p>Thanks for all your input ahead of time, let me know if you don&#39;t understand my stance on the subject and i&#39;ll clearify as needed !</p>",
